{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Information Theory Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Information content and entropy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def information_content(p, base=2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if p <= 0 or p > 1:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return float('inf') if p <= 0 else 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return -math.log(p) / math.log(base)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def entropy(probs, base=2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return sum("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        p * information_content(p, base)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for p in probs if p > 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "fair_coin = [0.5, 0.5]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "biased_coin = [0.99, 0.01]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "fair_die = [1/6] * 6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Fair coin entropy:   {entropy(fair_coin):.4f} bits\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Biased coin entropy: {entropy(biased_coin):.4f} bits\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Fair die entropy:    {entropy(fair_die):.4f} bits\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Cross-entropy and KL divergence"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def cross_entropy(p, q, base=2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for pi, qi in zip(p, q):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if pi > 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if qi <= 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                return float('inf')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            total += pi * (-math.log(qi) / math.log(base))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return total"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def kl_divergence(p, q, base=2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return cross_entropy(p, q, base) - entropy(p, base)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "true_dist = [0.7, 0.2, 0.1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "good_model = [0.6, 0.25, 0.15]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "bad_model = [0.1, 0.1, 0.8]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Entropy of true dist:     {entropy(true_dist):.4f} bits\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"CE (good model):          {cross_entropy(true_dist, good_model):.4f} bits\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"CE (bad model):           {cross_entropy(true_dist, bad_model):.4f} bits\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"KL divergence (good):     {kl_divergence(true_dist, good_model):.4f} bits\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"KL divergence (bad):      {kl_divergence(true_dist, bad_model):.4f} bits\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Cross-entropy as classification loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def softmax(logits):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    max_logit = max(logits)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    exps = [math.exp(z - max_logit) for z in logits]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total = sum(exps)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [e / total for e in exps]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def cross_entropy_loss(true_class, logits):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    probs = softmax(logits)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return -math.log(probs[true_class])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "logits = [2.0, 1.0, 0.1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "true_class = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "probs = softmax(logits)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "loss = cross_entropy_loss(true_class, logits)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Logits:      {logits}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Softmax:     {[f'{p:.4f}' for p in probs]}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"True class:  {true_class}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Loss:        {loss:.4f} nats\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Perplexity:  {math.exp(loss):.2f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Cross-entropy equals negative log-likelihood"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import random"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "random.seed(42)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "n_samples = 1000"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "n_classes = 3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "true_labels = [random.randint(0, n_classes - 1) for _ in range(n_samples)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model_logits = [[random.gauss(0, 1) for _ in range(n_classes)] for _ in range(n_samples)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "ce_loss = sum("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    cross_entropy_loss(label, logits)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for label, logits in zip(true_labels, model_logits)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ") / n_samples"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "nll = -sum("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    math.log(softmax(logits)[label])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for label, logits in zip(true_labels, model_logits)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ") / n_samples"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Cross-entropy loss:      {ce_loss:.6f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Negative log-likelihood: {nll:.6f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Difference:              {abs(ce_loss - nll):.2e}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Mutual information"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def mutual_information(joint_probs, base=2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rows = len(joint_probs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    cols = len(joint_probs[0])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    margin_x = [sum(joint_probs[i][j] for j in range(cols)) for i in range(rows)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    margin_y = [sum(joint_probs[i][j] for i in range(rows)) for j in range(cols)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mi = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(rows):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for j in range(cols):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            pxy = joint_probs[i][j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if pxy > 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                mi += pxy * math.log(pxy / (margin_x[i] * margin_y[j])) / math.log(base)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return mi"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "independent = [[0.25, 0.25], [0.25, 0.25]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "dependent = [[0.45, 0.05], [0.05, 0.45]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"MI (independent): {mutual_information(independent):.4f} bits\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"MI (dependent):   {mutual_information(dependent):.4f} bits\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Compute the entropy of the English alphabet assuming uniform distribution (26 letters). Then estimate it using actual letter frequencies. Which is higher and why?\n\n2. A model outputs logits [5.0, 2.0, 0.5] for a sample with true class 1. Compute the cross-entropy loss by hand, then verify with your `cross_entropy_loss` function. What logits would give zero loss?\n\n3. Show that KL divergence is not symmetric. Pick two distributions P and Q and compute D_KL(P || Q) and D_KL(Q || P). Explain why they differ.\n\n4. Build a function that computes perplexity for a sequence of token predictions. Given a list of (true_token_index, predicted_logits) pairs, return the perplexity of the sequence."
      ]
    }
